This is how BGP communities are used in AWS:

BGP - This is a protocol where routes are exchanged with 2 or more autonomous systems.

An example will be AWS and a customer router.

eExtra metadata (labels/tags) attached to advertised prefixes.

Well known predefined including 

- No_Export - Don’t advertise to EXTERNAL peers (AWS use this for incoming)
- No_ADVERTISE - Don’t advertise to any peers
- Regular communities = 32 bit value, split into 2 x 16
- AS_NUMBER:OPERATOR_ASSIGNED_VALUE
- i.e 7724:9100…. 7224:8100
- BGP operators (you or AWS) act on advertisement based on communities

